abstract: >
  Code, trained checkpoints, experimental results, statistical analysis pipeline, and
  camera-ready figures for a master's thesis evaluating a heterogeneous GNN+PPO policy
  on flexible job-shop scheduling (JSSP/FJSP), tested for static competitiveness (H1),
  size generalization (H2), robustness under three disruption types (H3), a
  disruption-aware reward mechanism (H4), and decision latency against CP-SAT (H5).
  Five pre-registered hypotheses were tested against frozen decision rules; four were
  rejected and one accepted, each diagnosed to a concrete, reported root cause rather
  than left as an unexplained negative result.
